# Build warnings that are known and harmless, one regular expression per line, then " # " with
# why it is harmless and a date to look at it again. scripts/check-build-log.mjs reads this; CI
# fails on any other warning. Keep it short.

# Payload logs this when no email key is set, as in CI, where nothing should be sent. Review 2027-04
No email adapter provided  # CI has no email service on purpose; production refuses to start without one. Review 2027-04

# Each CI run starts on a fresh machine with no .next folder, so there is no cache to reuse. Vercel
# keeps its own cache between deployments. Review 2027-04
No build cache found  # CI builds from scratch on purpose; Vercel caches its own builds. Review 2027-04
